<div id="body" class="mktoText" style="font-family: Helvetica, Arial, Sans-Serif; padding:10px;">
<p>Hi {{lead.First Name:default=Friend}},</p> 
<div>
Flywire 
<a href="https://www.flywire.com/resources/report-pulse-on-payments-2022-b2b-payments-outlook?utm_source=marketo&amp;utm_medium=email" target="_blank" id="">recently surveyed 300 of your finance peers</a> working at companies with both global and US-only based operations about their Accounts Receivable (A/R) and payment processes. It is clear that many businesses today have focused too hard on the Accounts Payable (A/P), taking away much-needed focus on A/R. 
<br />
<br /> Flywire’s 
<a href="https://www.flywire.com/resources/report-pulse-on-payments-2022-b2b-payments-outlook?utm_source=marketo&amp;utm_medium=email" target="_blank" id="">latest industry report</a> explores key findings like: 
<br /> 
<ul> 
<li>How A/R processes are holding back profitability</li> 
<li>How foreign exchange rates and collections struggles hinder global expansion</li> 
<li>Why cybersecurity, integrated technology remain major challenges</li> 
</ul> One of the most surprising findings in our survey was that 92% of respondents believe they could increase their earnings-per-share (EPS) if they had a better handle on their A/R processes. 
<br />
<br /> Thank you, 
<br />Josh Easterly
</div> 
